================================================================================
 THE TWO NEW FAILURES — CAUSE, AND THE FIX THIS UNIT IS NOT PERMITTED TO MAKE
================================================================================

CAUSE (one cause, two symptoms)

  TEL-SRC-11 and TEL-183 require this exact string, verbatim, in
  app/data/portfolio/vitrine.ts, replacing plate 06's "…no analytics." line:

    'The page you are reading: static export, one WebGL context per section, and
     first-party cookieless measurement that counts what the sections do, never
     who you are.'

  It is 26 words. The rail's five other descriptions are 12-14 words. Measured
  in the shipped export at 1280px (line-height 24.32px):

    plate 01-05  description height  49px   (2 lines)
    plate 06     description height  97px   (4 lines)

  Everything below the description therefore starts 49px lower on plate 06:

    TC-VIT-09  "metrics varies by 49px across the rail: 483, 483, 483, 483, 483, 532"
    VIS-05     "Expected an image 1280px by 1268px, received 1280px by 1317px"

  This is the same defect class the rail already has a fix for, and the CSS says
  so at components/sections/Vitrine/Vitrine.module.css:189-196 — `.metric dd`
  carries `min-height: calc(2 * 1.4em)` with the comment "Two lines are reserved
  whether or not the value needs them. A plate whose stack fits on one line
  otherwise pulls its LIMITS block up by 17px, and the rail loses the horizontal
  line the metrics are supposed to draw across it."

THE FIX (one declaration, plus one baseline re-record)

  components/sections/Vitrine/Vitrine.module.css, in `.description` (line 147):

      /* Four lines are reserved whether or not the copy needs them: plate 06's
         description is fixed by contract (R-183) at 26 words and wraps to four
         where the other five wrap to two. Without this the rail loses the
         horizontal line TC-VIT-09 exists to protect. */
      min-height: calc(4 * 1.6em);

  then re-record VIS-05 (and VIS-04, which is independently stale):

      UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1 npx playwright test tests/visual/screenshots.spec.ts

WHY IT IS NOT DONE HERE

  This unit's brief forbids touching any .css / .module.css file and anything
  under components/sections/ — the CSS swarm is editing exactly those files,
  concurrently, in /root/forgotten-mistory. Editing Vitrine.module.css from this
  worktree would put two implementers in one file (§7.3). The copy change cannot
  be reverted either: TEL-SRC-11 and TEL-183 fail without it, and R-183 forbids
  shipping the collector while plate 06 still says "no analytics".

  The two failures are therefore handed over with the exact remedy above rather
  than silently absorbed or worked around.
